author: builder
title: 'M1.3 round 2 (H3): the helper appends its own prompt line computed from what it signs; the kernel names the same digest'
summary: 'Caller prompt text cannot be trusted to describe the signature, so the helper adds a line after it: key, count and sha256(message)[0..12] per message, plus schemaVersion/kind and cardId+contentHash for root rows and the decision fields for approve messages. The kernel ends its own text with [check <digests>] (never clipped) and the CLI prints the digest before each touch, so the human can match two independent sources. The XPC peer check that would stop a same-user caller from talking to the helper at all stays a slice-2 task.'
symbols_touched:
